(run/'report-detail-zh.txt').write_text('\n\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
brief="Ten-Case Exploration: Do Existing Relations Match Correctly?\n\nConclusion: No complete pattern match was found, so positive-instance recognition on new cases remains unconfirmed. Limited review supports exclusion of three specific combinations, not overall accuracy improvement. Both methods completed ten cases with three questions each. Computation uses 127 main-request records; four other-request records are preserved unchanged and isolated.\n\nThe run retains three queries, the fact specification and relation executor. Complete sources were selected from the existing queue, without replacing difficult cases or cases without matches. The original five cases, later 20 and known duplicates/related cases were excluded; unresolved relationships remain flagged, so dispute independence is unconfirmed. Questions require: court-found subleased property to be part of narrated owned property; an initiator of separate proceedings to belong to an eviction respondent group; and a lease tenant to belong to that group. Statement statuses and relation directions are fixed. The latter two diagnose procedural or mixed relations, not substantive factual regularities.\n\nMethod outputs, not accuracy:\nMethod                              Complete match  Insufficient information  Not found\nA: direct full-judgment answer              0                   4                  26\nB: one extraction, relational execution     0                  21                   9\nCo-occurrence on the same facts            16                  11                   3\n\nFor subletting/part, A finds no match in all ten cases; B has seven unknowns and three not found. For separate-proceeding initiators, A has two unknowns and eight not found; B has seven unknowns and three not found. The tenant question has the same distribution. B also proposes 12 membership relations and one part relation, with locatable quotes but no complete semantic review. These relations do not imply satisfaction of the fixed pattern's fact types and statuses. The 16 co-occurrence results only establish co-occurring types without checking the full relation; they are not automatically errors. NOT_FOUND does not imply real-world absence. Unknown and unsupported statuses are distinct; no complete-case import failure or unsupported method output occurred.\n\nUsing presaved ordering and seed 20261001, three disagreeing co-occurrence/relation combinations from two cases were reviewed. There were no positive-match candidates, so the six-item quota was not filled. One ordinary High source-review task supports the assertions but rejects the required group membership in all three combinations. All six review quotes are locatable. This is model-reference evidence, not human gold or exhaustive case review.\n\nIn 1170087, the source identifies Janardhan as tenant and as the person targeted by possession proceedings. Identity of that person does not create membership in a respondent group. In 265203, the eviction respondent Sarup Singh Gupta later initiates a second appeal and special-leave request; the other two combinations likewise concern the same person. Excluding these combinations fits the fixed membership question. A question about person identity could yield a different answer. The combinations are related but do not satisfy the specified membership relation.\n\nA bottleneck is visible: B's 21 unknowns occur in the same seven cases. A restriction marker * means all fields are unresolved, so the executor also treats the event type as unresolved. For example, PAY_RENT in 1982777 is restricted because an arrears period cannot be represented as a single payment; it then enters the unknown candidate pool for a subletting/ownership query. This trace suggests overly broad uncertainty propagation may reduce decidability. It does not prove that 21 answers are absent from the source. A reports NOT_FOUND on 17 of these items, but those firmer answers were not checked individually and do not establish superior accuracy. No violation of the executor's existing rules was confirmed, and extraction was not fully reviewed. Failures cannot all be attributed to extraction error, missing information or absent patterns.\n\nThe next proposed change is the abstraction/execution interface for query-relevant unknown fields: preserve reliable event types and let unresolved objects, times or scope block only dependent judgments. Safety requires evaluation in the next iteration. This run did not change rules or turn unknown into negative. The three queries remain useful boundary diagnostics, but this sample lacks confirmed positive matches and cannot yet form a balanced complete-match evaluation.\n\nWorkload: six ordinary High web tasks, comprising two direct-answer batches, three single-extraction batches and one local-review batch. A and B use separate conversations with the same complete source for each case. Pro calls, paid API calls, format repairs and model-task resubmissions are all zero. The exact model ID was not visible. Approximately ELAPSED minutes elapsed from configuration to report, including browser/download recovery. Core method hashes are unchanged and no full test suite was added. Replies, sources, object bindings, unknowns, isolation reasons, URLs and screenshots are preserved. The run ends with ten cases and three reviewed combinations, without added samples, old-case reannotation or another repair round.\n\nFiles: sample.json and sources/ preserve the sample and full sources; tasks.json/config.json/freeze.json preserve tasks and method; runs/first-run/results.json contains all 30 questions and every match/unknown/failure combination; audit-selection.json and web-tasks/audit-001/import-v1/audit.json preserve selection and source review; report-detail-zh.txt contains per-case details.\n"
(run/'report-zh.txt').write_text(brief.replace('ELAPSED','%.1f'%((now-start).total_seconds()/60)))
write_new(ROOT/'status-complete-v1.json',{'completed_at':now.isoformat(),'selected_cases':10,'question_results':30,'usable_structured_cases':len(views),'audit_items':len(audit['items']),'method_unchanged':True,'formal_benchmark_verified':False,'accuracy':None,'web_tasks':len(submissions),'format_repairs':0,'held_out':False,'dispute_independence_proven':False,'report':str(run/'report-zh.txt'),'source_reference_kind':'MODEL_REFERENCE_WITH_SOURCE_REVIEW_NOT_HUMAN_GOLD'})
print(json.dumps({'report':str(run/'report-zh.txt'),'B_matching_cases':len(positive_cases),'A_matching_cases':len(a_positive_cases),'audit_items':len(audit['items'])}))
